# 22. Inspect's actual role across everything

Inspect should be boring infrastructure.

One runtime:

```text
Inspect
```

running:

```text
T1-EVAL
ARGMAP-EVAL
L2-EVAL
L200-EVAL
C1-EVAL
TANTRAFACT
```

It supports custom/multiple scorers, offline rescoring and separate scanner-style checks, so this is exactly the appropriate use. ([Inspect][7])

Do not create:

```text
T1 benchmark runner
L2 benchmark runner
L200 benchmark runner
TantraFact runner
...
```

as parallel orchestration systems.

Inspect owns execution/logging.

Pāṭala owns the scorers/contracts/data.

